│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ efficient_ansatz_reorg                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ I am optimizing the ansatz structure to improve both parameter efficiency and state-space │
│                          │ exploration. The original ansatz used three layers of single-qubit rotations (RY-RZ-RZ)   │
│                          │ leading to 24 parameters per block and 146 total parameters.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ My proposal replaces this with two layers of distinct single-qubit rotations (RY and RX)  │
│                          │ separated by two layers of CZ entanglement, creating a more entangled, compact structure  │
│                          │ with only 16 parameters per block (total 98 parameters). This maintains the overall       │
│                          │ connectivity (a full 0-1-2-3-4-5-6-7 chain) while significantly increasing parameter      │
│                          │ efficiency, which is a key component of the `combined_score`. By using RY and RX          │
│                          │ rotations, we ensure better exploration of the Bloch sphere compared to just RY/RZ.       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
