│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduce_ansatz_params_by_pairing                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ To improve the parameter efficiency and potential generalization of the model, I am       │
│                          │ introducing parameter sharing across qubit pairs for all single-qubit rotation layers (RY │
│                          │ and both RZ layers). The current implementation uses 24 unique parameters per ansatz      │
│                          │ block. By pairing qubits (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), and (6,7) and sharing parameters between    │
│                          │ them, we reduce the number of unique parameters per block to 12. This significantly       │
│                          │ reduces the total parameter count while maintaining the same circuit architecture, which  │
│                          │ typically improves training stability and parameter efficiency without degrading          │
│                          │ accuracy.                                                                                 │
