│ patch_description        │ Replace the current fully-local RX/RZ + sparse CRZ ansatz block with a more               │
│                          │ parameter-efficient, symmetry-aware structure:                                            │
│                          │ - Share RY parameters within each qubit pair (0,1),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7): 4 params instead of │
│                          │ 8.                                                                                        │
│                          │ - Share RZ parameters within each qubit pair: 4 params instead of 8.                      │
│                          │ - Use one parametrized CRZ per qubit pair with pair-local parameters: 4 params (same      │
│                          │ count as before for entanglers, but now aligned with the shared single-qubit structure).  │
│                          │ - Keep a fixed CZ entangling ladder to preserve nontrivial connectivity and expressivity  │
│                          │ without adding parameters.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters per block (from 20 -> 12), improving parameter efficiency while   │
│                          │ maintaining (pairwise) entangling structure that works well with the fixed 2-qubit        │
│                          │ feature encoding and re-uploading.                                                        │
