│                          │ 3. Implementing parameter sharing between paired qubits (0-1, 2-3, etc.) to improve       │
│                          │ efficiency                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. Adding more expressive local rotations with pre- and post-entanglement RZ layers       │
│                          │ 5. Utilizing CRZ gates for parametrized cross-talk between qubit pairs                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach combines the benefits of hardware-efficient ansätze with more sophisticated │
│                          │ entanglement patterns. The structure is designed to improve gradient flow while reducing  │
│                          │ the total parameter count, leading to faster convergence and better generalization.       │
